INT. IRON LUNG BOXING GYM - RING - NIGHT

Ropes sagged to the ankle. A bell with a cracked rim. A crowd of forty on folding chairs. The overhead bulb sways.

BIRDIE SOLOMON, 60s, trainer, towel on his neck, kneels in the corner. Opposite, KAI DRAKE, 25, champion, in a gold robe, jabs at air. In the other corner, a MASKED FIGHTER, 30s, lean, silver wrestling mask, shakes out his arms.

MC ROLAND PRYCE, 50s, in a ruffled shirt, taps a microphone.

MC
Ladies and gentlemen, in the red corner, a mystery!

The crowd murmurs. Bell. The Masked Fighter and Kai circle. Jab, jab, a feint, a hook. Kai tags him on the chin. The Masked Fighter staggers. Birdie winces.

BIRDIE
Elbows up, son!

Kai swings again. The Masked Fighter ducks. Their gloves tangle. They clinch. Both freeze, panting. Kai grabs the silver mask and rips it off.

Beneath is a face the whole room knows. LUCIAN DRAKE, 30s, Kai's older brother, missing seven years.

KAI
Lucian?

LUCIAN
Little brother.

KAI ^
You're dead.

LUCIAN ^
Not tonight.

Birdie drops his towel. The MC drops the microphone. The crowd goes silent.

Lucian raises his gloves. Kai, after a long moment, lowers his. They stand there, two men with the same jaw, in a ring too small for either.
